    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1053">

                <pb facs="1046" n="1034" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg1034"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115A Pacific War/1166: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-16">May 16,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received May 16—9:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3114. American Interests—Japan. Department’s 554, March 8, 1943.<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d1053-f1"/> Swiss Minister, Tokyo, reports first payment effected 22
                    Americans [on] Guam. While awaiting receipts which Japanese Government requested
                    obtain, husbands interned Kobe signed promissory notes. Gorgé inquires whether
                    may continue such payments or await assurance recipients received
                        payment.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d1053-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1053-f1" n="60" xml:id="d1053-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1053-f2" n="61" xml:id="d1053-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 1792, May 23, to Bern, the Department authorized continuation of
                    payments and requested that Mr. Gorgé make every effort to obtain receipts
                    (740.00115 Pacific War/1166).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
